-- title:
--   Finite p-power codimension of the [p]-series forces characteristic p
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $p$ a prime, and $d$ a natural number. Let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $k$ in the sense of [`MvFormalGroup d k`](def/MvFormalGroup_BasicV2.html#L15): a family $F_1,\dots,F_d$ of formal power series in the $2d$ variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,d$, each with vanishing constant term, with the coefficient of the first-copy variable $X_{\mathrm{inl}\,j}$ in $F_i$ equal to $\delta_{ij}$ and likewise for the second-copy variable $X_{\mathrm{inr}\,j}$, and satisfying the associativity identity $F(F(X,Y),Z) = F(X,F(Y,Z))$ as $d$-tuples of power series in $3d$ variables. For $n \in \mathbb{N}$ let `F.nthSeries n` be the $n$-fold iterate defined by `F.nthSeries 0 = 0` and `F.nthSeries (n+1) i = F_i(\,`F.nthSeries n`\,, X)`, i.e. the multiplication-by-$n$ series $[n]_F$ of $d$ power series in $d$ variables. Assume that for some $h$ the $k$-vector space $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,d, k)$ modulo the ideal generated by the $d$ components of $[p]_F$ has `Module.finrank` over $k$ equal to $p^h$, and that $h \neq 0$. Then $k$ has characteristic $p$.
--
--   This is the standard observation that a formal group law of finite height over a field can only exist in characteristic $p$: the linear part of $[p]_F$ is $p$ times the identity, so if $p$ were invertible the ideal generated by $[p]_F$ would be the maximal ideal and the quotient would have dimension $1$, contradicting dimension $p^h$ with $h \neq 0$. It is used in the construction of deformation functors for special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_charP_of_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_eq_pow.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MvFormalGroup_BasicV2

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open MvPowerSeries in

theorem MvFormalGroup.charP_of_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_eq_pow
    {k : Type u} [Field k] (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] {d : ℕ} (F : MvFormalGroup d k) (h : ℕ)
    (hh : Module.finrank k (MvPowerSeries (Fin d) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range (F.nthSeries p))) = p ^ h)
    (h0 : h ≠ 0) : CharP k p := by sorry
